  body: "# Pension and bereavement benefits in forfeiture referrals\n\n## Source-backed proposal\n\nThe chapter
    describes forfeiture-referral contexts involving WB, BB, BSP, SP or RP based wholly or partly on a deceased
    spouse’s or civil partner’s contributions, with further inheritable-component cases.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\
    \nThe list does not mean every pension held by the person is automatically forfeited. An own-right pension without
    an advantage from the death is distinguished in DMG 76004. No equivalence with Pension Credit or Universal Credit
    is asserted.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 76008, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a81fada40f0b6230269a321/dmgch76.pdf#page=4).\n\
    - [DMG 76032, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a81fada40f0b6230269a321/dmgch76.pdf#page=6).\n\
    - [DMG 76033, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a81fada40f0b6230269a321/dmgch76.pdf#page=6).\n\
    \n## Provenance and review\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of DWP guidance, not an official DWP document.
    All definitions and relationships are model-assisted and unreviewed. No individual eligibility, award, legal
    conclusion or executable rule is supplied.\n\nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, stated
    legal date and pension event date have separate meanings. PDF page numbers are one-based file positions; extraction
    may damage reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n-
    `dmg-vol12-ch76` — PDF SHA-256 `074f2d3f00d4886954d5cbd6ba2653ec407c1ff9f0160a0ca74d337227f9f542`; page-extraction
    SHA-256 `53eb7c5ec81ced813ac2faf2af9f772c5f3e9662112a7ef678dcb4daef0b73f8`.\n"
