      quote: "76032    Where there is reason to believe that\n\n         1.    a person has been, or is likely to
        be charged with their spouse's or civil\n               partner’s murder, manslaughter or culpable homicide
        and\n\n         2.    the person’s claim for WB, BB, BSP, SP or RP is based wholly or partly on\n      \
        \         their late spouse’s or civil partner’s contributions\n\n         the DM should send the claim
        to DMA Leeds as soon as possible with the\n         documents in DMG 76029."
      locator: DMG 76032
  - target: term/rp-old-pension-regime
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source expressly includes RP and separately discusses inheritable components; it does not
      forfeit all own-right RP.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch76/0006
      quote: "76032    Where there is reason to believe that\n\n         1.    a person has been, or is likely to
        be charged with their spouse's or civil\n               partner’s murder, manslaughter or culpable homicide
        and\n\n         2.    the person’s claim for WB, BB, BSP, SP or RP is based wholly or partly on\n      \
        \         their late spouse’s or civil partner’s contributions\n\n         the DM should send the claim
        to DMA Leeds as soon as possible with the\n         documents in DMG 76029."
      locator: DMG 76032
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch76/0006
      quote: "76033    The DM should also send to DMA Leeds a claim received from a widower whose\n         entitlement
        to benefit arises directly from his unlawful act of murder or\n                                        \
        \                                       1\n         manslaughter. The benefit affected is an IB(LT) or a
        Category A RP .\n\n         Any case in which the survivor's RP entitlement would normally be increased
        on\n         account of inheritable components should be sent to DMA Leeds.\n                          \
        \                                                         1 SS CB Act 92, s 41"
